WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.689
Tactics, techniques, and procedures, often called TTPs, describe behavior patterns.

2
00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:14.299
In defensive profiling, behavior matters because it can support detection and readiness even when attribution remains uncertain.

3
00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:20.603
A label may change or be disputed, but repeated behavior can still tell defenders what to monitor.

4
00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:35.670
Initial access patterns, credential abuse at a high level, lateral movement concepts, persistence concepts, command-and-control concepts, data access patterns, and impact patterns can all support a behavior-focused profile.

5
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:41.052
Frameworks such as ATT&CK can help analysts organize observations conceptually.

6
00:00:41.052 --> 00:00:48.586
Mapping behavior to a framework gives teams a shared language for detection planning, reporting, and gap analysis.

7
00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:51.891
But framework mapping is not proof of attribution.

8
00:00:51.891 --> 00:00:54.505
Many actors can use similar techniques.

9
00:00:54.505 --> 00:01:00.271
Commodity tools and common operational patterns can appear across unrelated activity.

10
00:01:00.271 --> 00:01:04.345
The map helps organize evidence; it does not replace judgment.

11
00:01:04.345 --> 00:01:08.881
AI can help extract TTP observations from reports and incident notes.

12
00:01:08.881 --> 00:01:18.490
It can group behaviors by phase, compare observed activity to known profiles, identify missing evidence, and draft summaries for detection teams.

13
00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:29.176
The analyst should still verify that the model did not over-map vague language, merge unrelated cases, or treat a report's conclusion as stronger than its evidence.

14
00:01:29.176 --> 00:01:34.865
The best AI-assisted TTP work keeps original references close to each mapped behavior.

15
00:01:34.865 --> 00:01:38.555
Behavior-based profiling supports practical defense.

16
00:01:38.555 --> 00:01:52.393
If a profile shows recurring use of certain access methods, operational timing, target types, or post-compromise goals at a high level, defenders can prioritize monitoring and readiness around those behaviors.

17
00:01:52.393 --> 00:01:55.544
The point is not to publish a dramatic actor name.

18
00:01:55.544 --> 00:02:03.078
The point is to produce a defensible picture that helps security teams prepare for what the actor is likely to do next.
